  annotation "note_1771577549154_1", anchor: "a genealogical tome whose last three entries turned opaque, as though examined and marked by something within the sealed passages", text: "I noted in my Crystalline Lineage annotation that Grandmother Deep's reconnaissance into penguin bloodline records was conducted for theological purposes — the Accord judiciary established as much and asked no follow-up questions. Now whatever occupies the sealed passages where Mairae~ drove the corruption is conducting its own genealogical research, examining lineage entries and marking them opaque. One earnestly hopes these are unrelated projects. The alternative — that corruption driven into the deep has developed *curatorial instincts* about bloodline data — deserves more attention than the single documented case this entry provides. I would check the tome myself, but I suspect touching it is precisely the experiment someone is waiting for.", type: :commentary, display: :full
